<Base title="khensu shell" description="Specifications for the khensu shell for iPhone 18 Pro: a battleproof titanium or brass shell that turns your iPhone into a node.">
  <p class="eyebrow">khensu shell</p>
  <h1>Your phone becomes part of the network</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    One shell for iPhone 18 Pro, Pro Max and 18, in your iPhone’s colour, matte titanium or solid brass. It turns the phone into a
    node with its own battery, and finishes level with the lenses, so your iPhone is no thicker at its thickest point.
  </p>

  <h2>Specifications</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Specification</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Fits</td><td>iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max. Coming to iPhone 18 when it arrives.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Thickness</td><td>4.2 mm on the back, level with the lens tops: +0 mm at the iPhone’s thickest point. A flat back, with only the lenses showing.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Footprint</td><td>71.1 × 149.2 mm, inset from the phone’s outline and following its edge curve, so it never overhangs</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Shell</td><td>CNC-machined grade 5 titanium for a precise fit, matte powder coat in Burgundy, Glacier, Silver or Black. Or bare solid brass (C26000), which darkens to a natural patina.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Weight</td><td>About 87 g in titanium, 126 g in brass</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Battery life</td><td>About 5 hours as a node on its own battery, then it runs from your iPhone over USB-C</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Charging</td><td>USB-C. Charges the shell and passes power to your iPhone.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Attachment</td><td>Micro-suction film and MagSafe-compatible magnets</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Antennas</td><td>A band in the edge, so nearby nodes reach each other directly where there’s no internet</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Camera</td><td>Clears every lens, flash and sensor</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="footnote">
    Figures for iPhone 18 Pro, from the current CAD model on placeholder geometry, until Apple’s accessory drawings are
    available; production figures may change. iPhone and MagSafe are trademarks of Apple Inc.
  </p>

  <h2>Inside</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Part</th><th>Hardware</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Node computer</td><td>NXP i.MX 93 system-on-module (Arm Cortex-A55), 2 GB LPDDR4X, 32 GB eMMC</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Network guard</td><td>STMicroelectronics STM32U5 (Arm Cortex-M33 with TrustZone), running open Rust firmware with post-quantum secure boot</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mesh radio</td><td>Wi-Fi HaLow (802.11ah) module based on the Morse Micro MM6108</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Wi-Fi and Bluetooth</td><td>Wi-Fi 6 and Bluetooth LE 5.3</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Battery</td><td>6 Wh single-cell lithium-ion pouch, 3.85 V, shaped to the shell, with on-board protection and temperature sensing</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Power</td><td>USB-C Power Delivery, dual role, with power-path charging and a fuel gauge</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Board</td><td>34 × 14 × 1.6 mm</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="footnote">
    Current design choices; parts may change before production. NXP, i.MX, STMicroelectronics, STM32, Morse Micro,
    Arm, Cortex, TrustZone, Wi-Fi HaLow and Bluetooth are trademarks of their respective owners.
  </p>

